        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/foote/{size}/1877_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-10-23T20:16:56.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Powerhound_2000\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/powerhound_2000/48/1859_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Powerhound_2000:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>There is also the fact in her bio there is this rumor.</p>\n<div>Quote:<br><blockquote>Others say that Kaargra struck a deal with some unfathomable cosmic entity, trading the portion of her soul that knew of mercy and kindness in exchange for power and a realm of her own in the form of the Bloodsworn Colosseum\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote></div>\nit is called a Relic Spirit and Kaarga possibly gave up part of her soul.\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I have not read such an interesting theory on these boards in a long time (I blame myself for not creating any new FooteNotes threads in a while). Even though this strikes me as unlikely, it strikes me none the less.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Strong work OP! There might just be something to this.</p>",
